  "fails_first": "Input offset of documented op-amp macromodels. OPA171 V_OS=214 uV is about 10x the Exp 22 analog bound. High open-loop gain does not remove the ~142x (1+Rf G_tot) multiplier on o2. GWL DC OP singularity is a model-convergence failure on the same loaded TIA, reported separately.",
  "easiest": "Programmable open-loop A on XSPICE limit / O-VF, and leakage at nA-class on the isolated cell. Isolated o2 |z|<2 V also fit inside \u00b13.3 V L rails.",
  "remains_ideal": "Inverts stay high-A VCVS. ReLU stays a B-source. Fine-bank dest=0 compensation is unchanged. O-VF/L have no transistor dynamics. Architecture I dump remains the numerical exact VG.",
  "hardware_level": "LEVEL 2 structured (O-VF, L) and LEVEL 3 macromodel (OPA171, MCP6041). Not LEVEL 4-6. Not board power. Not silicon. O-VF is not a high-Z OTA.",
  "limitations": "OPA171 needs ngspice PSpice IF() compatibility. MCP6041 is a 6 V part. O-VF sets rout=1 ohm so A=gm*rout survives Rf; that is a voltage op-amp equivalent. IN+ trim is a known-model voltage, not a replica, and would not cancel uncorrelated per-chip Vos. Isolated MAE vs z is not full-network MAE. GWL 1 F capacitors forbid UIC as a DC method.",
  "final_status": "OFFSET-LIMITED VG PRIMITIVE",
  "conclusion": "OFFSET-LIMITED VG PRIMITIVE. XSPICE L/O-VF meet analog MAE on Network A (and F) at Vos=0, matching Exp 17 behavioral TIA. Documented LEVEL 3 OPA171/MCP6041 do not meet the 22 uV analog offset spec. IN+ trim on Network A changed MAE from 1.2974e-02 to 7.0311e-03, still above 1e-3. Isolated o2 trim MAE_z=2.6247e-01 (worse than untrimmed). Calibration of one zero-input Vsum does not restore the loaded worst neuron (Exp 19 lesson). Injecting 214 uV into L on F gives analog MAE=7.5467e-03 (above 1e-3). Full Network F OPA171 MAE=1.4932e-01 acc=7.5000e-01: analog fails and classification drops. That is worse than L+214 uV because Vsum on o2 reaches ~10 mV, so the macromodel is not holding virtual ground under Rf G_tot=141.",
